Now implement the `retrieveUserData()` method:

```php
private function retrieveUserData(string $accessToken)
{
    $key = 'auth:' . hash('sha256', $accessToken);
    $userData = $this->redis->get($key);

    if ($userData === false) {
        try {
            // Call the external API using the access token and handle transient errors with retries.
            $retriedUserData = $this->rettr->get(
                'https://api.example.com/user-data', [
                    'query' => [
                        'access_token' => $accessToken,
                        // Add other necessary parameters here.
                    ],
                ]
            )->onError(function ($e) {
                if ($e->getCode() === Rettr\RettrException::RETRYABLE_ERRORS[0]) {
                    sleep($this->backoffDelay());
                    return true;
                }

                throw $e;
            })->send()->wait();

            if (!$retriedUserData->isSuccessful()) {
                // Handle API errors here.
            }

            $userData = json_decode($retriedUserData->getBody(), true);
            $this->redis->setex($key, $this->cacheExpiration, json_encode($userData));
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            // Log the error for future debugging.
        }
    }

    return $userData;
}
```

Finally, create a factory for the AuthService to make it easier to register and use:

