For the Java function to read a JSON document and extract nested fields based on a user-defined path specification:

```java
import org.json.JSONObject;

public class JsonPathExtractor {
    public static Object getJsonValue(String json, String path) {
        JSONObject obj = new JSONObject(json);
        return getJsonValue(obj, path);
    }

    private static Object getJsonValue(JSONObject obj, String path) {
        if (path.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Path cannot be empty");
        }

        String[] parts = path.split("\\.");
        JSONObject currentObj = obj;

        for (String part : parts) {
            if (!currentObj.has(part)) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Path does not exist: " + path);
            }

            currentObj = currentObj.getJSONObject(part);
        }

        return currentObj.get(parts[parts.length - 1]);
    }
}
```

This function can be utilized within the data pipeline to extract and enrich metadata from JSON documents received in real-time.']

