[' Due to the complexity of the task and the constraints you've provided, I'll break down my response into several parts: Java method, Webpack configuration, and testing strategies.

1. Java Method (DeserializeByteArray.java):

```java
import java.io.*;
import javax.naming.ServiceNotFoundException;
import java.lang.IllegalArgumentException;
import java.lang.ClassNotFoundException;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock;

public class DeserializeByteArray {
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<String, Class<?>> classMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private static final ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();

    public static <T> T deserialize(byte[] data) {
        try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(data))) {
            Class<?> clazz = classMap.getOrDefault(ois.readUTF(), null);
            if (clazz == null) {
                throw new ServiceNotFoundException("Class not found in the current classpath: " + ois.readUTF());
            }
            return (T) ois.readObject();
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid or corrupted data.", e);
        }
    }

    public static void registerClass(String name, Class<?> clazz) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            classMap.put(name, clazz);
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }
}
```

