- Implement fallback strategies for external service failures to maintain directory integrity and minimize disruption to end-users.

5. DOM Traversal Function (using a recursive approach)

```javascript
function findElementsBySelector(root, selector, predicateFunction) {
    const found = [];
    const traverse = (node) => {
        if (node === null || node.nodeType !== 1) return; // Ignore non-element nodes and text nodes

        if (predicateFunction(node)) {
            found.push(node);
        }

        Array.from(node.children).forEach((childNode) => traverse(childNode));
    };

    traverse(root);
    return found.filter((element) => element.matches(selector));
}
```

This function accepts a root element, a selector string, and a predicateFunction that tests whether an element matches the specified criteria (based on class or ID). It efficiently traverses the DOM structure, identifies matching elements, and returns them for further processing."]

